{
  "configuration_id": "config_039",
  "reason": "Evidence: The best result so far is config_015 (scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l + transformer + weighted, multiprofile) at 0.725 accuracy, with config_033 (transformer+concat, 0.721) and config_034 (avgpool+concat, 0.715) close behind. This clearly establishes scvi_n200 as the superior RNA encoder and transformer+weighted as the best aggregation/fusion pairing. All scvi_n200 + ViT-L + multiprofile combinations are now tested. Question: This experiment tests whether the best aggregation strategy (transformer + weighted) transfers to ResNet50 as the image encoder, completing the design-space picture for the top RNA encoder. It also reveals whether a cheaper image backbone could approach ViT-L's performance with this aggregation. Rationale: As the final experiment, this is the most informative remaining test—it pairs the two best-validated components (scvi_n200, transformer+weighted) with the only untested image encoder in the multiprofile setting, confirming whether ViT-L is essential or whether ResNet50 offers a cost-effective near-equivalent. Expected relative cost: moderate-to-low (~2.5–3.5 GPU hours), since ResNet50 is a smaller backbone than ViT-L, making this cheaper than config_015 (3.60 hrs) while still providing a definitive answer on the image-encoder axis."
}

